t e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=e^{u}+C$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 x^{3} + 3$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(6 x^{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 3 x^{2} e^{2 x^{3} + 3}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(e^{u}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}\\left(e^{2 x^{3} + 3}\\right)+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679259 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "caf1d597-c130-5150-a713-e088d5003d84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{3}\\left(e^{3 - 2 x^{3}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679286}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "caf1d597-c130-5150-a713-e088d5003d84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- \\frac{2}{3}\\left(e^{3 - 2 x^{3}}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679286} :answer-field/id #uuid "bc07202b-066e-5a08-88ea-66ff3182e51f" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679282}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "91154a9a-ca11-54f8-a6c6-dd9021a1ba24" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int 4 x^{2} e^{3 - 2 x^{3}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=e^{u}+C$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=3 - 2 x^{3}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(- 6 x^{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 4 x^{2} e^{3 - 2 x^{3}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=- \\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{2}{3}\\left(\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=- \\frac{2}{3}\\left(e^{u}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n- \\frac{2}{3}\\left(e^{3 - 2 x^{3}}\\right)