{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=- x^{2}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(- 2 x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int 4 x e^{- x^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=-2\\left(\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n-2\\left(\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=-2\\left(e^{u}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n-2\\left(e^{- x^{2}}\\right)+C.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186679307 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "437f1665-9174-56cd-afe9-d40705cdf224" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\left(e^{2 x^{2} + 2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "437f1665-9174-56cd-afe9-d40705cdf224" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}\\left(e^{2 x^{2} + 2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679234} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a960b19-9d30-5fff-9769-bfc8766836c3" :answer-field/key "answer" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186679221}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e85dd74f-6dd4-57d9-b36f-4d1d2828023a" :question/problem "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int x e^{2 x^{2} + 2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=e^{u}+C$.\n\n{{answer}} $+C$" :question/worked-solution "Let $u=2 x^{2} + 2$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(4 x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int x e^{2 x^{2} + 2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}\\left(\\int e^{u}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=\\frac{1}{4}\\left(e^{u}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{4}\\left(e^{2 x^{2} + 2}\\right)+C.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Integrating Products Containing the Exponential Function"}]}
